Rāvaṇa sends beloved prince Akṣa against Hanumān --- Akṣa rides jeweled chariot to tōraṇa monkey --- Akṣa pierces Hanumān head with three arrows --- Akṣa showers arrows and Hanumān roars and grows --- Hanumān admires Akṣa valor then resolves to kill --- Hanumān smashes eight horses and chariot with palms --- Hanumān seizes Akṣa by feet whirls and dashes him down --- Gods marvel as Hanumān retakes tōraṇa